    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping sequence numbers entirely. All values derived from the customer code follow through to the new identity.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (which built `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` from a per-city sequence count) with `buildCustomerCode(owner, normalizedTelephone)`.\n- `REGION` comes from a new `deriveRegion(postcode, city)` helper: postcode range first (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), then the city table, then `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n- `HASH8` comes from a new `sha256Hex8(...)` helper \u2014 the first 4 bytes / 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`.\n- The audit record (`AUDIT.info(... customerCode=...)`) already reads `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now emits the region-and-hash code automatically (verified in the log: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and `checkDigit` (Luhn over the digits in the customer code) already derive from `customerCode`, so they now build on the new identity with no logic change.\n- `locality` now sources the `REGION` segment directly from the customer code, falling back to the old postcode/city derivation only when no customer code is present.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples to reflect the new format.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` (asserting the code matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) passes.",
